{"uid":"modules/lazy_feedmatch.py","name":"lazy_feedmatch.py","qualname":"modules/lazy_feedmatch.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/lazy_feedmatch.py","line":1,"end_line":527,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Exploit feed matching for LazyOwn.","description":"Turns a local exploit-intelligence feed into per-product evidence decisions\nfor the services the engagement has already discovered. A product name alone\nis never evidence: only a version inside a bounded affected range of the same\nproduct counts, with one deliberate exception for actively exploited\nadvisories that publish no usable range (kept as low-confidence review\ncandidates, never counted as heat). Products seen with no version stay as\nunversioned leads so a later banner, probe or host report can promote them.\n\nTier maths live in :mod:`modules.lazy_heat` (the one vocabulary: hot/warm/\ncold); this file adds the feed schema, the sighting binding and the live\nadapter to :mod:`modules.lazy_cve_feed`. Feed schema (JSON file, default\n``sessions/intel/exploit_feed.json``)::\n\n    {\"entries\": [\n        {\"cve_id\": \"CVE-2024-0001\", \"product\": \"apache tomcat\",\n         \"cvss\": 9.8, \"kev\": true, \"epss\": 0.42, \"public_exploit\": true,\n         \"ranges\": [{\"introduced\": \"10.0.0\", \"fixed\": \"10.0.20\"}],\n         \"references\": [\"https://...\"]},\n        ...\n    ]}\n\nStdlib only, pure functions on plain input, never raises on bad data.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::DEFAULT_FEED_PATH","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::EVIDENCE_IN_RANGE","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::EVIDENCE_UNBOUNDED","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::EVIDENCE_NONE","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::RANGE_KEYS","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::FeedEntry","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::Sighting","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::ExploitSighting","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::load_feed","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::parse_feed","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::is_os_sighting","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::entry_matches_product","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::version_in_ranges","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::feed_tier","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::bind_sighting","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::unversioned_leads","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::live_bindings","modules/lazy_feedmatch.py::feed_fingerprint"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
